From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:33:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D221 server: an agent lookup waits for the location's plugins

Upstream: GET /api/agent/:agentID answers as soon as the location is built, before its plugins have registered the
agents and applied the config to them, while GET /api/agent waits (#59082). As a location's first request,
GET /api/agent/general answers 404 AgentNotFoundError, and GET /api/agent/build answers a half-built agent: the
built-in definition without the config's model, description or color.
Fixed: the lookup waits for plugin activation like the list (503 ServiceUnavailableError when it times out,
now declared). GET /api/provider/:providerID stays nonblocking: upstream kept it so on purpose in #59082, and its
test asserts it ("single provider reads stay nonblocking").
Scenarios: project-agents.test.ts "agent lookups on a location's first request" (new)
Upstream tests: packages/server/test/agent-get.test.ts (new); client and openapi.json regenerated

